\f1\fs22 At around four on Christmas morning, his device woke him, hailing him as said king of said world, and wrenching him  from a lovely dream. \'93What the tax?\'94\
\'93It\'92s Dr Ortolan,\'94 Dr Ortolan said, as even-tempered as ever.\
\'93Really? I thought it was Santa\'92s elves confirming they\'92d delivered my Nobel Peace Prize to the stocking on my mantelpiece.\'94\
\'93For your lifelong commitment to team morale? I think it\'92s still in internal mail.\'94\
\'93Don\'92t be a smart-dick, Ortolan.\'94\
Ortolan drew a breath. \'93I\'92d thought you\'92d want to know\'85 someone\'92s downloaded a software upgrade to the Washing Machine.\'94\
\'93What? Well it wasn\'92t me.\'94\
\'93Yes, well, you are not exactly software are you?\'94\
\'93Software is for minions, Ortolan. Dispensable, replaceable, like cogs in an atomic clock.\'94\
Ortolan took another breath. \'93You\'92d better get down here.\'94\
\'93I can\'92t. I\'92m locked out.\'94\
\'93No you\'92re not. I saw you in the Lysander.\'94\
\'93No, you didn\'92t.\'94\
\'93If you could have seem the look on your face when Sarah and Hayley rescued Eloise.\'94\
Johnny flushed with embarrassment, and was glad Ortolan hadn\'92t made a vid call. When it was obvious the gates weren\'92t coming down, Johnny helped himself to one of the guest suites in the mansion.\
\'93Give me twelve minutes.\'94
